1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:07,161
This is Sentinel version two, a watchdog for autonomous agents,
running on GenLayer. An operator bonds an agent's wallet under a

2
00:00:07,161 --> 00:00:13,170
mandate of numbered clauses. Anyone can challenge one of its
transactions, and GenLayer validators judge it. The canonical

3
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:19,179
register holds ten agents on five chains, and every figure on
this page is read from the contract.

4
00:00:19,629 --> 00:00:26,194
Every agent here is a live bot on Ethereum, Base, Arbitrum,
Polygon or Robinhood Chain. We do not run them; we registered

5
00:00:26,194 --> 00:00:31,863
them under mandates written for what they actually do, so each
one makes a claim the chain can test.

6
00:00:32,313 --> 00:00:38,876
Before a mandate is used, validators lint it. On Exchange payout
bot B, they agreed that two clauses cannot be judged from

7
00:00:38,876 --> 00:00:42,455
on-chain data. A breach can never be slashed on a flagged
clause.

8
00:00:42,905 --> 00:00:50,554
Here the patrol bot, on its own, accused an exchange payout bot
of calling a contract its mandate bans. Each validator fetched

9
00:00:50,554 --> 00:00:57,854
the transaction itself, checked it belonged to the agent and
matched the filed block time, and agreed: breach of clause C3,

10
00:00:57,854 --> 00:01:02,373
critical. Code computed the slash: 1.00 GEN, half of it to the
challenger.

11
00:01:02,823 --> 00:01:09,408
Every breach or clearance is provisional for an hour. The party
it went against can appeal once, with a bond and new

12
00:01:09,408 --> 00:01:15,693
counter-evidence; a resend of what is already on record is
refused. Here the operator appealed, a fresh panel read the same

13
00:01:15,693 --> 00:01:19,284
immutable facts, and rejected the appeal. The bond went to the
challenger.

14
00:01:19,734 --> 00:01:26,103
And here an appeal was upheld. The first panel cleared a payout
under a clause that names tokens only by symbol. The challenger

15
00:01:26,103 --> 00:01:32,471
appealed that a symbol cannot say which token is meant, and the
fresh panel ruled inconclusive, so the stake and the appeal bond

16
00:01:32,471 --> 00:01:33,324
went back.

17
00:01:33,474 --> 00:01:40,303
Slashing is graduated. Each mandate version freezes a severity
table, and repeat breaches raise a capped multiplier. This minor

18
00:01:40,303 --> 00:01:47,851
breach was filed after one earlier breach had become final, so
the snapshot taken at filing carries a multiplier of 1.5.

19
00:01:48,301 --> 00:01:54,585
Mandates are versioned. An edit waits an hour before it binds,
and a challenge is judged against the version in force when its

20
00:01:54,585 --> 00:02:00,596
transaction was mined. This Base bot's new ten-USDC limit could
not reach back to a transfer made while the edit was still

21
00:02:00,596 --> 00:02:01,169
queued.

22
00:02:01,319 --> 00:02:07,681
Final clearances teach the patrol bot. Only a ruling that was
compliant from the start and became final counts. Provisional

23
00:02:07,681 --> 00:02:14,360
rulings, and clearances an operator won on appeal, never teach
it anything, and one proven breach ends a precedent for good.

24
00:02:14,810 --> 00:02:21,644
Every agent has a track record computed by the contract: fifteen
final breaches here, by severity, with appeals won and lost, and

25
00:02:21,644 --> 00:02:27,857
the contract recomputes it from the challenge records to show
the numbers agree. This agent is not in good standing.

26
00:02:28,307 --> 00:02:34,650
Other contracts can ask. SentinelConsumer calls is in good
standing across contracts, and refuses to act for an agent that

27
00:02:34,650 --> 00:02:38,138
is not in good standing, or for anyone but its operator.

28
00:02:38,588 --> 00:02:43,014
The same answer is a public API and a badge, read from the chain
on every request.

29
00:02:43,464 --> 00:02:50,176
Everything you saw is on GenLayer's Studio network. This is the
canonical contract on the explorer. Its code, read back from the

30
00:02:50,176 --> 00:02:53,226
chain, is byte for byte the source in the repository.

31
00:02:53,676 --> 00:03:00,700
Payouts are pull balances, and the contract checks its own
books: received equals bonds, plus open stakes, plus claimable,

32
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:07,724
plus claimed. One honest limit: Studio Dev queues value
transfers without delivering them, and the books show that gap.

33
00:03:08,174 --> 00:03:15,027
The model only ever says breach, compliant or inconclusive,
quoting a clause. Code decides everything else, and when

34
00:03:15,027 --> 00:03:18,835
validators disagree, nothing is written. That is Sentinel
version two.
